<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Per-model accuracy by condition (100% compliant, first-pass). <math id="S3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> in parentheses. Model names abbreviated from Section 2.1. Three patterns emerge: (1) models with low control baselines show the largest constraint gains (Gemini Flash Lite: +15.7 pp for No-Have; Sonnet: +13.3 pp for elaborated prompt); (2) models near ceiling show minimal movement (Haiku: 93.0% control, +3.2 pp max); (3) two OpenAI models show flat or negative effects under E-Prime specifically, while still benefiting from shallower constraints.</figcaption>
</figure>
