<td id="S3.T4.2.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S3.T4.2.7.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Partial</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Per-model condition rankings (treatment conditions only, 100% compliant). “Depth inversion” = shallowest constraint (neutral ban) outperforms deepest (E-Prime). The pattern holds cleanly in 3 of 6 models. Sonnet reverses it entirely; GPT-4o-mini and Flash Lite show mixed profiles. E-Prime ranks last in 4 of 6 models.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Of 70 pooled pairwise comparisons, 14 survived FDR correction at <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. (These <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values assume trial-level independence; see Section 5, “Item-level dependence,” for why this is anti-conservative. The headline effects are large enough to be robust, but comparisons near the <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> threshold should be interpreted with caution.)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Depth Inversion</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The central finding of this paper is the inverse relationship between the theoretical depth of a constraint and its effect on accuracy:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.SS2.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S3.SS2.tab1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Constraint</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Theoretical Depth</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracy</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Delta vs. Control</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Neutral filler-word ban</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Shallowest (no inference role)</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">89.7%</span></td>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+6.7 pp</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">No-Have</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Moderate (possessive framing)</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">88.4%</span></td>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+5.4 pp</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Elaborated prompt</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">None (metacognitive only)</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">87.2%</span></td>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+4.2 pp</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">E-Prime</span></th>
<th id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Deepest (copula, identity, existence)</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">86.7%</span></td>
<td id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.SS2.tab1.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+3.7 pp</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The theoretical depth ranking is derived from linguistic function, not assigned post hoc. E-Prime removes the copula, the verb class that encodes predication, identity, and existence, which are foundational to logical inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Korzybski, 1933</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bourland, 1965</a>]</cite>. No-Have removes possession and experiential verbs, which participate in framing but are less central to logical structure than the copula. The elaborated prompt adds metacognitive scaffolding without targeting any vocabulary. The neutral ban removes intensifiers and hedges, words that modulate emphasis but play no role in propositional logic. This ordering (E-Prime <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> No-Have <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> elaborated prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> neutral ban, from deepest to shallowest) follows from the degree to which each intervention engages with inference-relevant linguistic structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Adopting this ordering as a hypothesis, the data show a monotone inversion: the four conditions rank in perfect inverse order of theoretical depth by effect size. (With only four data points, this ordering is descriptive, and a formal rank correlation would be uninformative at this <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, but the monotone pattern is striking against the cognitive restructuring prediction, which requires the opposite direction.) The depth inversion is contingent on this theoretical ranking; alternative orderings might weaken the pattern, though the extremes (E-Prime smallest, neutral ban largest) are robust to reordering of the middle conditions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This is the opposite of what cognitive restructuring predicts. If removing reasoning-relevant vocabulary forces more explicit reasoning, E-Prime should outperform the neutral ban. Instead, the relationship runs precisely backward.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Significant Pairwise Comparisons</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fourteen of 70 pooled comparisons survived FDR correction. The significant results cluster in four task types:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Classification.</span> Neutral ban (+7.6 pp vs. control, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.395" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.395</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.395</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>) and No-Have (+6.7 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.320</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.320</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>) both significantly outperform control and elaborated prompt. E-Prime also outperforms control (+4.8 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.201" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.201</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.201</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.026" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.026</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.026</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ethical dilemmas.</span> No-Have (+18.1 pp vs. control, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.522" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.522</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.522</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>), neutral ban (+15.7 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.430" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.430</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.430</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.003" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.003</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.003</annotation></semantics></math>), E-Prime (+13.3 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.353" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.353</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.353</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.007" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.007</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.007</annotation></semantics></math>), and elaborated prompt (+11.1 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.284" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.284</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.284</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.005</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.005</annotation></semantics></math>) all significantly outperform control. No-Have also significantly outperforms elaborated prompt (+7.1 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.029</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Epistemic calibration.</span> Elaborated prompt (+18.5 pp vs. control, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.429" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.429</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.429</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>) dominates this task. No-Have significantly underperforms the elaborated prompt (<math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-10.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-10.9</annotation></semantics></math> pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.003" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.003</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.003</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Causal reasoning.</span> Elaborated prompt (+10.0 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.254" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.254</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.254</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.021" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.021</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.021</annotation></semantics></math>) and neutral ban (+10.5 pp, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=0.269" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.269</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=0.269</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.029" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.029</annotation></semantics></math>) significantly outperform control.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">No pairwise comparison in syllogisms or math word problems reached significance, consistent with ceiling effects (<math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>92% control accuracy) limiting detectable differences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Prediction Check</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The prospective directional predictions for E-Prime (Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1.4 Prospective Predictions ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Trivial Vocabulary Bans Improve LLM ReasoningMore Than Deep Linguistic Constraints" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) achieved 5/7 accuracy: causal reasoning, epistemic calibration, ethical dilemmas, math word problems, and syllogisms matched predicted directions. Analogical reasoning (predicted improvement, observed <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-6.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-6.5</annotation></semantics></math>%) and classification (predicted degradation, observed +4.8%) were incorrect. Five of seven is better than chance but not significantly so (binomial <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.23</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.23</annotation></semantics></math> against a 50% base rate), and far from the pattern-level confirmation the cognitive restructuring hypothesis required.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">More critically, the prediction framework was designed for E-Prime specifically and has no account of why the neutral word ban or the elaborated prompt should produce comparable or larger effects.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Cross-Model Correlation Does Not Replicate</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Paper 1 reported cross-model correlations of E-Prime task effects reaching <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=-0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=-0.75</annotation></semantics></math>, interpreted as evidence of a structural constraint signature. In the present study with six models:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.SS5.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S3.SS5.tab1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model Pair</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="S3.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (E-Prime)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Haiku vs. Sonnet</span></th>
<td id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">+0.336</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.SS5.tab1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
