<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Mean word count by condition and task (first-pass, 100% compliant).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The elaborated prompt consistently produces the longest responses (17–56% longer than control). Vocabulary-constrained conditions produce shorter responses than control (8–34% shorter). This dissociates length from accuracy: the neutral ban produces the highest accuracy with below-control word counts, while the elaborated prompt produces longer responses with lower accuracy than the neutral ban.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.8 </span>E-Prime Retry Analysis (Supplementary)</h3>

<div id="S3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">E-Prime’s overall retry rate was 45.6% (1,231/2,700 trials). Retry rates varied dramatically by model:</p>
</div>
